# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Deep Research Agent — environment configuration
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in your own keys. NOTHING here is required
# to import the package; you only need keys for the sources/models you use.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── LLM (required for the `multi` profile — the cheap cloud default) ──────────
# OpenRouter routes the multi-model profile (Gemini Flash / DeepSeek / etc).
# Get one at https://openrouter.ai/keys
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-your-openrouter-key-here

# ── Direct Anthropic fallback (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────
# Used only if OpenRouter returns 402 (out of credits) or is unreachable.
# Must be a real API key (sk-ant-api...), NOT a CLI OAuth token (sk-ant-oat...).
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY_SUB1=sk-ant-api03-your-anthropic-key-here
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-api03-your-anthropic-key-here

# ── Web search (strongly recommended — the backbone source) ───────────────────
# Brave Search API. Free tier available. https://brave.com/search/api/
BRAVE_API_KEY=BSA-your-brave-search-key-here

# ── Deep page extraction (optional but recommended) ───────────────────────────
# Firecrawl scrapes full content from the top web results. https://firecrawl.dev
FIRECRAWL_API_KEY=fc-your-firecrawl-key-here

# ── GitHub source (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A classic PAT raises rate limits for repo/code/issue search. https://github.com/settings/tokens
GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_your-github-token-here

# ── X / Twitter source (optional — high-fidelity, dated tweets) ───────────────
# twitterapi.io — ~$0.15 / 1k tweets (pennies per run). https://twitterapi.io
# Without this, the X tool falls back to sparse, undated Brave site-search.
TWITTERAPI_IO_KEY=your-twitterapi-io-key-here

# ── Reddit source (optional — high-fidelity, recent posts) ────────────────────
# Free "script" app at https://www.reddit.com/prefs/apps (any redirect URI works).
# Without these, the Reddit tool falls back to sparse Brave site-search.
REDDIT_CLIENT_ID=your-reddit-client-id-here
REDDIT_CLIENT_SECRET=your-reddit-client-secret-here
# Reddit asks for a descriptive User-Agent. Recommended format:
# "<platform>:<app id>:<version> (by /u/<your-username>)"
REDDIT_USER_AGENT=deep-research-agent/1.0 (by /u/your_username)

# ── Local LLM (optional — the `multi` profile's local worker step) ────────────
# If you run Ollama locally, the cheap profile offloads the "observations" step
# to it. Defaults to http://localhost:11434 if unset.
# OLLAMA_LOCAL_URL=http://localhost:11434
# OLLAMA_LOCAL_MODEL=llama3.1:8b
# OLLAMA_REMOTE_URL=http://192.168.1.50:11434   # a beefier box on your LAN, optional

# ── Output (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where finished Markdown reports are written. Defaults to ~/deep-research-reports.
# Point it at an Obsidian vault, a synced folder, anywhere you like.
# DEEP_RESEARCH_OUTPUT_DIR=~/deep-research-reports
# DEEP_RESEARCH_CHECKPOINT_DIR=~/.deep-research/checkpoints

# ── Progress streaming (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Stream live progress to a Telegram chat during a run (--notify flag).
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=your-telegram-bot-token-here
# TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=your-telegram-chat-id-here
